 critical negative regulator of p53</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2004</year><volume>429</volume><fpage>86</fpage><lpage>92</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Nature||429|86||bib4|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15103385</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gartel</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Feliciano</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Tyner</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A new method for determining the status of p53 in tumor cell lines of different origin</article-title><source>Oncol Res</source><year>2003</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>405</fpage><lpage>408</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Oncol Res||13|405||bib5|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12725531</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>DR</given-names></name><name><surname>Evan</surname><given-names>GI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A matter of life and death</article-title><source>Cancer Cell</source><year>2002</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer Cell||1|19||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12086884</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hao</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Sekine</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kawabata</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakamura</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Ishioka</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohata</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Katayama</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hashimoto</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Noda</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsuruo</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Naito</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Apollon ubiquitinates SMAC and caspase-9, and has an essential cytoprotection function</article-title><source>Nat Cell Biol</source><year>2004</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>849</fpage><lpage>860</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Nat Cell Biol||6|849||bib7|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15300255</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hong</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Lei</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Glas</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tumors acquire inhibitor of apoptosis protein (IAP)-mediated apoptosis resistance through altered specificity of cytosolic proteolysis</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>197</volume><fpage>1731</fpage><lpage>1743</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Exp Med||197|1731||bib8|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12810691</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Janicke</surname><given-names>RU</given-names></name><name><surname>Sprengart</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name><name><surname>Wati</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name><name><surname>Porter</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Caspase-3 is required for DNA fragmentation and morphological changes associated with apoptosis</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1998</year><volume>273</volume><fpage>9357</fpage><lpage>9360</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Biol Chem||273|9357||bib9|'--><pub-id pub-i